    "Reason : 1 - The Local Planning Authority is not satisfied, on the balance of probabilities, that the evidence submitted demonstrates that the use of the premises as a residential dwelling forming the basis of this application, has subsisted continuously or lawfully for a period of 10 years as required under Section 171B of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).  On this basis, the Local Planning Authority is not persuaded that the use as a dwelling is therefore lawful and refuses to issue a Certificate of Lawful Existing Use under Section 191 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).    "
